  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale  \n   The solution adopts a **simulated annealing** algorithm to minimize the maximum overlap integral. Unlike the parent solution's local search, this approach explores both structural changes (cyclic shifts) and small local perturbations (controlled mass swaps) while maintaining entropy to escape local optima. The core intuition is that global shifts disrupt aligned intervals, while local swaps fine-tune mass distribution. Key innovations include temperature-based move selection and adaptive delta adjustments to balance exploration versus exploitation.  \n\n2. Mathematical specification  \n   **Variables**: Represented as a piecewise constant function \\(h(x)\\) over \\([0,2]\\) by \\(n\\) samples with \\(0 \\leq h[i] \\leq 1\\) and \\(\\sum_i h[i] \\cdot \\frac{2}{n} = 1\\) (integral enforcement via projection).  \n   **Constraints**: Projections ensure feasibility after structural moves.  \n   **Objective**: Minimize \\(C_5 = \\max_k \\text{np.correlate}(h, 1-h, \\text{mode}=\\text{'full'}) \\cdot \\frac{2}{n}\\) (maximum overlap integral).  \n   **Simulated annealing**:  \n   - **Moves**:  \n     - *Global*: Cyclic shifts (\\(\\approx\\) structural transitions).  \n     - *Local*: Mass swaps (controlled \\(\\pm \\delta\\) between indices).  \n   - **Transition probabilities**: Metropolis criterion with temperature decay.  \n   - **Termination**: Steps until time budget exhausted.  \n\n3. Implementation procedure  \n   - **Feasibility projection**: Clipping and integral adjustment.  \n   - **Objective computation**: Compute overlap integral per lag.  \n   - **Simulated annealing loop**:  \n     - Select moves randomly (80% local, 20% global).  \n     - Update with acceptance probability proportional to \\(e^{-\\Delta C_5 / T}\\).  \n     - Adjust temperature \\(T\\) exponentially (\\(T_{\\text{new}} = \\alpha \\cdot T_{\\text{old}})\\).  \n     - Include delta scaling (\\(\\delta \\propto \\sqrt{T}\\)) to maintain exploration.  \n   - **Fallback**: Return best solution if budget exhausted.  \n\n4. Search choices and variations  \n   - **Move selection**: Local (80% probability) for gradient escape; global (20%) for structural changes.  \n   - **Temperature decay**: \\(\\alpha = 0.998\\) with minimal \\(T_{\\text{min}} = 0.1\\).  \n   - **Delta adjustment**: \\(\\delta = \\epsilon \\sqrt{250} \\cdot \\sqrt{10T}\\) to balance scale.  \n   - **Key parameters**:  \n     - \\(\\epsilon = 0.01\\), \\(\\alpha = 0.998\\).  \n     - Initial \\(T_0 = 10\\), steps \\(= 100 \\cdot n_{\\text{budget}}\\).  \n     - Lag computation: `compute_c5(h, n)`.  \n\n5. Compute budget and robustness  \n   - **Time control**: Steps per second derived from fix\\`n = 250\\` (1100 steps\u00b7s\\(^{-1}\\)).  \n   - **Termination check**: Every 100 steps assess \\(C_5\\) for stagnation.  \n   - **Fallback**: Clipped solution if integral constraint violated.  \n   - **Complexity**: \\(O(\\text{steps} \\cdot \\text{project}_{\\text{feasible}} + \\text{steps} \\cdot \\text{compute\\_c5})\\).  \n\n6. Validation and return contract  \n   - **Feasibility**: `validate_feasibility(h)`: \\(\\sum_i h[i] = n/2\\) and \\(0 \\leq h[i] \\leq 1\\).  \n   - **Objective**: `compute_c5` for final candidate.  \n   - **Output**: \\(C_5\\) lower than parent (\\(< 0.3808)\\).  \n   - **Sanity checks**:  \n     ```python\n     assert np.isfinite(best_c5)\n     assert 0 <= best_h.min() <= 1\n     assert best_h.sum() == n/2\n     ```  \n   - **Example**: Parent `initial_h_values` passed with \\(C_5 \\approx 0.3808\\).  \n\n**Implementation steps summary**:  \n1. Initialize `h` from parent (n=250).  \n2. Set parameters \\(T_0 = 10, \\alpha = 0.998\\), \\(\\epsilon = 0.01\\).  \n3. `while T > 1e-3 and time < deadline`:  \n   - Randomly choose move type and index.  \n   - Update `h` with cyclic shift or mass swap.  \n   - Project new `h` and accept update based on \\(C_5\\) change.  \n4. Return best valid `h`, \\(C_5 \\approx <0.3808\\), and `n=250`.  \n\n**Error handling**:  \n- If shift violates bounds, retry with `[0, n-1]`.  \n- If \\(C_5\\) not improving for 500 steps, log and continue.  \n- Ensure \\(\\delta\\) stays within \\([10^{-6}, 1]\\).  \n\nThis approach explicitly improves global exploration while preserving the parent's structure.",
